# AI Interview Coach — Day 8 Summary

**Day:** 8 of 10 | **Focus:** Testing, Debugging & Production Optimization

## Senior QA/Security/Performance Review — Findings & Fixes

A full review was conducted before writing any code, covering bugs, edge cases, error handling, validation, API failures, empty/offline states, performance, duplicate code, and security. Findings, ranked by severity:

| # | Severity | Issue | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 🔴 High | All-or-nothing AI feedback fallback — one malformed JSON field discarded an entire real evaluation | ✅ Fixed — per-field safe coercion |
| 2 | 🔴 High | No score/confidence bounds validation — malformed AI output could show `score: 15` | ✅ Fixed — clamped to valid ranges, regression-tested |
| 3 | 🟠 Medium | No input length limits on JD/resume/answers — risk of API token-limit failures | ✅ Fixed — truncation at 4000/6000 chars, plus UI-level `max_chars` |
| 4 | 🟠 Medium | DB connections not guaranteed to close on exception | ✅ Fixed — context-managed connections with `try/finally` |
| 5 | 🟠 Medium | No indexes on foreign key columns | ✅ Fixed — indexes added on `session_id`, `question_id`, `answer_id` |
| 6 | 🟠 Medium | New Groq client created on every single API call | ✅ Fixed — `@st.cache_resource` caches the provider instance |
| 7 | 🟡 Low | Duplicated `session_state` key lists across files | ✅ Fixed — centralized in `core/session_utils.py` |
| 8 | 🟡 Low | No automated tests existed | ✅ Fixed — 28 tests added |
| 9 | 🟢 Info | SQL injection review | No issues — all queries parameterized |
| 10 | 🟢 Info | XSS review | No issues — user text never rendered with `unsafe_allow_html` |

